          "canonical_hash": "sha256:b72fbf2a8159af258b91faa56ec1bdf0bb402344e7673ea4409c3c1680c6e36d",
          "description": "Read-only introspection of the current vLLM launch flags. Prefers the LIVE process's real argv (/proc/<pid>/cmdline of the systemd unit's MainPID) as ground truth; falls back to the static exec script if the process isn't currently up. vLLM does not expose its own launch flags over the API, so this never queries the server itself. Any argv value following a flag matching a known-sensitive pattern (token/key/secret/password/credential) is redacted before being returned.",
